Linux has (by default) a 3GB brk limit for userspace programs, and can
overcommit memory for programs like this that allocate more than they
use. Windows doesn't, and I also think it has a 2GB brk limit.

(It has to; kernelspace can easily exceed 1GB on large systems, which
would make it bluescreen *hard*... waitaminute...)


Anyway, to make it work you'll have to decrease the malloc size manually,
and hope that no parts of the code has it hardcoded. Good luck...

